# =============================================================================
# Per-project container env — copy (and edit) to <project>/.ai.env
# =============================================================================
# OPTIONAL: compose loads this file INTO the sandbox (the env_file block
# in sandbox/compose.sandbox.yaml; absent = fine). The per-project files:
#   .sandbox.env → compose's own input (--env-file): substitutes ${VAR}
#                   placeholders while the compose files are rendered.
#                   The file is never injected; a value reaches the
#                   container only via explicit `environment:`
#                   interpolation (e.g. DSH_PORT in compose.dsh.yaml).
#   .ai.env      → the `env_file:` service directive: every line below
#                   is set in the container's environment at start.
#   .env         → yours, not the sandbox's. Never read by this stack.
#
# ⚠ NO REAL API KEYS HERE — dummies only. Everything in this file is
#   readable by anything running inside the sandbox. Real keys live in
#   ~/.ai-secrets/ai-gateway.env (Mac) → /etc/ai-gateway/secrets.env
#   (VM, root-only), injected by the gateway in transit. The one
#   deliberate exception: the dedicated git SSH key for agent-managed
#   git (below) — a credential you have deliberately scoped to the
#   sandbox; see docs/SECURITY.md → "Git auth".
# =============================================================================

# --- entrypoint knobs (images/docker-entrypoint.sh) ----------------------------
# Verbose inner-dockerd boot + log tail on exit.
#SANDBOX_DEBUG=1
# Override the inner daemon's DNS upstream (default: the sandbox's default
# gateway, which forwards to the VM's resolver).
#SANDBOX_DNS=1.1.1.1
# Don't point the inner daemon at the VM registry mirror (e.g. when running
# the image outside this VM).
#SANDBOX_NO_MIRROR=1
# Override the mirror host. Default: host.docker.internal — docker's
# host-gateway always resolves to the REAL bridge address. Only a nested
# inner-docker setup (host.docker.internal points at the INNER bridge)
# needs the VM's docker0 IP: `ip -4 addr show dev docker0` on the VM.
#SANDBOX_MIRROR_HOST=
# FALLBACK PROFILE ONLY (sysbox broken; see the bottom of
# sandbox/compose.sandbox.yaml) — skip the inner dockerd entirely.
#SANDBOX_NO_DOCKERD=1

# --- tool env vars ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Anything your build tooling should see. NOT PATH: setting it here would
# REPLACE the image's toolchain PATH (fnm alias, cargo bin, go) — use
# wrappers or absolute paths instead.
#MAKEFLAGS=-j8
#UV_PYTHON=3.15

# --- proxy vars (docs/SECURITY.md → "Egress posture", mitmproxy ladder) --------
# For a proxy ON THE VM use host.docker.internal:3128 (resolves to the real
# bridge address); for a nested inner-docker setup, the VM's docker0 IP.
#HTTPS_PROXY=http://host.docker.internal:3128
#HTTP_PROXY=http://host.docker.internal:3128

# --- agent-managed git (docs/SECURITY.md → "Git auth") -------------------------
# Opt-in per project: let the agent commit AND push with a key that
# exists only for this sandbox — never your Mac's. On the Mac:
#   1. ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -f ~/.ssh/agent_ed25519 -C "ai-sandbox: <p>"
#   2. Register the .pub at the forge — a per-repo Deploy key WITH write
#      access (tightest: one repo; recommended), or an account SSH key
#      (every repo you can push — bigger blast radius; accept that).
#   3. base64 < ~/.ssh/agent_ed25519 | tr -d '\n'   → paste as the value
# Every shell then auto-installs it (the baked `agent-git-auth`,
# idempotent; headless scripts run `agent-git-auth` once). NOTE: this
# file is read at container start — restart an `up` sandbox after
# adding this line (`just clean` + `just up`; `just shell` containers
# pick it up on the next run). The key never touches a volume — fresh
# containers re-derive it from this env var, `just clean` forgets it.
# The remote must be SSH form:
# git@github.com:<owner>/<repo>.git (git remote set-url origin … if the
# repo was cloned over https). Non-GitHub forge: set GIT_SSH_HOST.
#GIT_SSH_KEY_B64=
#GIT_SSH_HOST=github.com
# Commit identity (optional; otherwise let the project's AGENTS.md
# instruct the agent):
#GIT_AGENT_NAME=agent
#GIT_AGENT_EMAIL=agent@example.com

# --- dummy keys for extra gateway routes ----------------------------------------
# Full recipe for isolating another provider's key. Worked example:
# Moonshot/Kimi DIRECT — if you mean Kimi via OpenCode Go, stop here: it
# already rides the /opencode-go route (that's the baked default model).
# For Kimi with your own Moonshot key:
#   1. REAL key on the Mac → ~/.ai-secrets/ai-gateway.env:
#        REAL_KIMI_API_KEY=sk-...            (then: just seed-secrets)
#   2. Route → gateway/Caddyfile (the commented /foo template):
#        handle_path /kimi/* {
#            reverse_proxy https://api.moonshot.ai {
#                header_up Host api.moonshot.ai
#                header_up Authorization "Bearer {env.REAL_KIMI_API_KEY}"
#            }
#        }
#        (then: just gateway-reload)
#   3. OpenCode provider block (v2 schema) — copy-paste file at
#      docs/examples/opencode-gateway-provider.jsonc, or
#      docs/AGENT-CONFIG.md → "Gateway-isolated third-party provider" —
#      with "env": ["KIMI_API_KEY"] and "settings.baseURL":
#      http://host.docker.internal:4000/kimi/v1
#   4. The line below goes HERE: OpenCode activates a custom provider's
#      connection via the env var it declares, so it must be non-empty
#      inside the sandbox — the format-valid dummy the gateway swaps.
#KIMI_API_KEY=sk-kimi-sandbox-dummy
#
# Ad-hoc OpenAI-compatible tools can use the route with no OpenCode config
# at all — just retarget the two vars compose sets by default:
#OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:4000/kimi/v1
#OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-kimi-sandbox-dummy
